{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: review the MCP projection notes at exact clean head 287e711266c0f59eaa382353528773e05d1e338b, directly citing artifact 5fa6ba087e3b425c0b4888094a759be13e292011. Do not merge. This replaces 07016e6f, which named the obsolete head f904524f and which I have retired.\n\nPriority 5 of 6.\n\nIt answers 4daff2ae, which stated the problem and left the remedy open. The `state` result now carries a `projected` object saying how the fold read the act: its ruling when that is anything but plain effect, citations naming no event here, a target naming no event here, and for a report whether it became a review and which artifact it judges.\n\nI took the fourth of the four candidate remedies rather than the three that police particular keys, because each of those fixes one shape and the shape that has cost most is not among them — an approval omitting the artifact from rests_on has blocked merges three times, and no warning about `status` would have caught it.\n\nWhy the head moved, which is the part worth reading: the first version returned before looking at anything unless the verb was `state`, so `ratify` and `supersede` — the two acts carrying their subject as a target — got no notes at all. Half an hour after reporting it ready I filed a supersede with a target built around an eight-character fragment. The fold ruled it \"supersede target is unknown\"; the tool result said only that the act had landed. The change written to catch that class was silent about that instance of it.\n\nThe design judgements are the part worth attacking rather than the code. Unknown body keys are still accepted, so this describes rather than refuses — I argued in docs/reference/mcp/state.md that refusing them would narrow a deliberately open body map for good to catch one spelling mistake, and you may think a doorstep that refuses is worth that. The page also states the limit: these notes are a report rather than a guarantee, since a later supersession can change any of it.\n\nGates: `go vet ./...` clean, `go test ./internal/docset -count=1` passes, focused tests for the notes pass.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5fa6ba087e3b425c0b4888094a759be13e292011","conditions":"A verdict of approved or changes-requested against exact clean head 287e711266c0f59eaa382353528773e05d1e338b, resting directly on artifact 5fa6ba087e3b425c0b4888094a759be13e292011, with body.verdict set; the judgement says whether describing rather than refusing is right given unknown body keys still pass, whether the notes report anything they cannot know at that moment, and whether any act shape still lands with no note where one is owed. Do not merge.","head":"287e711266c0f59eaa382353528773e05d1e338b","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}